"2-ODE1OGJlNjEtMzRhYi00YjhjLTkyYWUtN2JhMjIyMTQ4MGM0XzEwMA==","Exciting opportunity at Codurance","Gabrielle Loureiro","https://www.linkedin.com/in/gabrielle-loureiro4515","Laércio Germano","https://www.linkedin.com/in/laerciogermano","2026-06-23 21:30:51 UTC","Exciting opportunity at Codurance","Hello!

I hope you’re doing well. My name is Gabrielle and I’m part of the Talent Acquisition team at Codurance. I noticed that you are open to work and believe your experience aligns well with a Full Stack Software Engineer opportunity we’re currently hiring for.

We’re looking for an engineer with solid React expertise who values pragmatism, professionalism, and transparency, and enjoys working in collaborative environments. The role involves building and maintaining scalable web applications with a strong focus on performance, clean architecture, and maintainability, across both greenfield and enterprise-grade systems.

Your background in developing and architecting high-load backend systems, especially with a focus on scalable APIs and cloud-native environments, could be a great asset to our team. Your experience with AWS and various programming languages, including PHP and TypeScript, complements the skill set we are seeking.

Key responsibilities:
Build and maintain robust Single Page Applications
Collaborate with product, design, and backend teams
Design and consume RESTful APIs
Contribute to scalable frontend architecture
Ensure quality through testing and CI practices

Requirements:
Strong React experience (hooks, state management, performance optimization)
Backend expertise (Golang, Python, Java, C# or .NET)
SPA knowledge (routing, caching, error boundaries, bundle optimization)
Experience with i18n and localization workflows
Familiarity with Design Systems and accessibility standards
Frontend testing experience (unit, integration, e2e)
Advanced/Fluent English

If this sounds interesting, send me your CV! I’d be glad to share more details and learn about your background.

Best regards,
Gabrielle

